 "applies_to": "Lochinvar Crest commercial condensing boilers with SMART SYSTEM Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
 "summary": "Gateway profile for the Lochinvar Crest: 59 objects (18 AI, 6 AO, 25 BI, 10 BO), 40 polled by default. Boiler Enable and Tank Thermostat are polled outputs; the rate/setpoint command, BMS temperature inputs and configuration bits are unpolled outputs. Inputs cover the safety switches, both flames and blowers, pumps, gas valves, temperatures, firing rate and the status, blocking and lockout codes.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Lochinvar_Crest_Boiler_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the Lochinvar Crest Modbus communication document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Lochinvar%20Crest%20Boiler%20Modbus%20Register%20List.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "Only 40 of the 59 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
  "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Tank Thermostat); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
 ],
